From 487c428ace6a7af6fdc90617caee704dd39d3332 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:28:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Enable the compiled XZ ARM64 filter on Windows

Select the latest registered XZ module, 5.4.5.bcr.9, and enable both ARM64 filter entry points in the Windows build configuration. This fixes the unused internal initializer without relaxing compiler diagnostics.

The focused Windows cross-build fails with arm64_coder_init unused before the change and succeeds afterward. The ARM64 filter compression/decompression regression passes on Linux; native Windows execution remains a hosted gate.
